Q: Why is flexbox justify-content: space-between not working on wider desktop screens A: <blockquote>
<p>I tried changing the flex shorthand values on the child elements</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That seems to be what's causing it in the first place.  To be clear, <code>space-between</code> <em>is</em> working.  But the two items are growing to fill available space.  (Save for the explicit <code>gap: 12px</code> between them of course.)</p>
<p>Removing those <code>flex: 2</code> and <code>flex: 3</code> rules allows them to be pushed further apart, which appears to be the effect you're looking for:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>section.hero {
  background: var(--dark-blue);
  color: var(--white);
  padding: 50px 8vw;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 12px;
}

.hero-lt {
  &amp; p {
    line-height: 1.1em;
    color: var(--off-white);
    font-weight: 300;
  }
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;section class="hero"&gt;
  &lt;div class="hero-lt"&gt;
    &lt;h1&gt;The Wonderful World of Bacteria&lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Ad, possimus?&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;button class="btn"&gt;Sign up&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="hero-rt"&gt;
    &lt;img src="https://picsum.photos/id/237/629/317" alt="Immune system fights bacteria"
                width="629" height="317"&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>Alternatively, if for some reason you want those boxes to continue filling available space, then it sounds like what you're asking isn't for more <code>space-between</code> but rather to <em>end-justify</em> the contents of the right-side container.  For example:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>section.hero {
  background: var(--dark-blue);
  color: var(--white);
  padding: 50px 8vw;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 12px;
}

.hero-lt {
  flex: 2;
}

.hero-lt {
  flex: 2;

  &amp; p {
    line-height: 1.1em;
    color: var(--off-white);
    font-weight: 300;
  }
}

.hero-rt {
  flex: 3;
  text-align: end; /* &lt;--- here */
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;section class="hero"&gt;
  &lt;div class="hero-lt"&gt;
    &lt;h1&gt;The Wonderful World of Bacteria&lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Ad, possimus?&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;button class="btn"&gt;Sign up&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="hero-rt"&gt;
    &lt;img src="https://picsum.photos/id/237/629/317" alt="Immune system fights bacteria"
                width="629" height="317"&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
